<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>For the wave <m>y = {3\sin 2x}</m>, where <m>x</m> is in degrees, find</p><div>(a) the amplitude <fillin characters="6" name="ans1"/>  </div><div>(b) the period <fillin characters="6" name="ans2"/> <m>^\circ</m>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) The amplitude is how far the wave rises above its mean line: the size of <m>{3}</m>, which is <m>{3}</m>.</p><p>(b) The period is how far along the axis before the wave repeats itself: <m>360^\circ \div {2} = {180}^\circ</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>3</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>180</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>